{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes between the two lotteries. In this case, the outcomes are: Lottery A offers 5000 Euros with 0.1% probability and 0 Euros with 99.9%; Lottery B offers 5 Euros with 100% probability. The pairwise difference in outcomes is |5000 - 5| = 4995 Euros. Since there is only one non-zero outcome in A and one fixed outcome in B, the sum of pairwise differences is simply the absolute difference between the outcomes (5000 and 5), which is 4995. This difference is the same regardless of probability weighting because the reason considers only the sum of outcome differences. Thus, the decision reason is applicable and can be evaluated using the outcome values.",
